# Mapbox Terrain-RGB token — get a free one at https://account.mapbox.com/
# (Tokens page, the default public token works fine). Optional: terrain
# features degrade gracefully with no crash if left unset (see
# getMapboxToken()/fetchTerrainTileCached() in src/lib/terrain/).
# On Vercel: if you set a URL-restricted token, restrict it to your deployed
# domain (Mapbox account → Tokens → edit → URL restrictions) — this is a
# public-type token that ends up in the shipped client JS regardless of
# where it's configured, so the restriction (not secrecy) is what limits abuse.
VITE_MAPBOX_TOKEN=

# YR/Frost/NIBIO/thredds requests are all proxied under /api/* — via Vite
# dev-server middleware locally (server/*Proxy.ts, vite.config.ts) and via
# equivalent Vercel serverless functions in production (api/*.ts). No
# environment-specific client code needed; the paths are identical either way.

# Frost API (frost.met.no) — real historical weather-station observations,
# used for genuine past-72h precipitation/temperature (vs. Locationforecast's
# forward-only forecast data used elsewhere in this app).
# Register a free client ID at https://frost.met.no/auth/requestCredentials.html
#
# SERVER-SIDE ONLY. Do NOT prefix with VITE_ — that would bundle it into the
# client JS. Proxied via /api/frost (server/frostProxy.ts locally, api/frost/*.ts
# on Vercel — both share the same handleFrostRoute logic).
# On Vercel: set this in Project Settings → Environment Variables, not in a
# committed file — it's only ever read server-side via process.env there.
# Leave unset to disable Frost entirely; the app falls back to the existing
# Locationforecast-derived values with no crash (see src/api/frostApi.ts).
FROST_CLIENT_ID=
